        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0783" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14708: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-02-16T13:00:00+08:00">February 16,
                            1939—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 16—10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. A letter dated February 15, addressed by the Japanese Consul General to the
                    Senior Consul quotes the following notice received by him from the Japanese
                    naval authorities: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Imperial Japanese Navy has decided to start shortly an operation at
                            Haimen at Taichow Bay, Chekiang Province, and its vicinity. It is
                            therefore requested that all the vessels of third powers now at or near
                            Haimen should evacuate by sunset on the 17th of February 1939 to a
                            distance sufficient to avoid danger, at least outside a radius of 30
                            nautical miles of Haimen.</p>
                        <p>The Imperial Japanese Navy will not hold themselves responsible for any
                            loss or damage sustained by any vessel remaining within the aforesaid
                            region after the specified time.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Interested American firms notified.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
